-80000-attend-launch-pop-up-of-teen-skin-care-brand-sincerely-yours/?_hsenc=
=3Dp2ANqtz-9elizNg9a0mxVXca4JaS5minyyZXB7Ye3FWFJM6vPSqB8sfx_m00OarhOzLHQ8Rz=
gXdIV9QTLl5y4lT_ZKPBJx6Yx41Q&_hsmi=3D397065654 ) people attend a Sephora-ho=
sted pop-up event in September. Its products sold out within the first hour=
.

- Others include Bubble Skin Care, Pipa, and Rini, which launched in Novemb=
er, founded by celebrity-entrepreneur Shay Mitchell.

These products are more expensive than traditional children=E2=80=99s optio=
ns =E2=80=94 e.g., Johnson=E2=80=99s baby lotion costs just ~$5, compared t=
o Evereden=E2=80=99s $28 moisturizer =E2=80=94 but cheaper than ones offere=
d by kid-favored adult brands, like Drunk Elephant=E2=80=99s $70 lotion.

Starting them young

The children=E2=80=99s cosmetics market, a global industry valued at ~$1.6B=
, is undeniable.

A 2024 study (https://ulta.a.bigcontent.io/v1/static/JoyProject_WK2124_Ulta=
BeautyReport?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9elizNg9a0mxVXca4JaS5minyyZXB7Ye3FWFJM6vPSqB8=
sfx_m00OarhOzLHQ8RzgXdIV9QTLl5y4lT_ZKPBJx6Yx41Q&_hsmi=3D397065654 ) by Ulta=
 Beauty found that, thanks to social media, kids now start toying around wi=
th beauty products by age 8. Whereas, for millennials and Gen Z, that didn=
=E2=80=99t happen until about ages 15 and 12, respectively.

On TikTok, young girls are mimicking older influencers with their own GRWM-=
style videos that showcase (https://www.nbcchicago.com/news/local/tiktok-sk=
incare-routines-for-teens-are-more-harmful-than-you-may-think-and-many-dont=
-contain-this-crucial-step/3763793/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9elizNg9a0mxVXca4JaS5m=
inyyZXB7Ye3FWFJM6vPSqB8sfx_m00OarhOzLHQ8RzgXdIV9QTLl5y4lT_ZKPBJx6Yx41Q&_hsm=
i=3D397065654 ) their extensive beauty routines.

But not everyone is happy about it

The beauty-for-babies trend has divided parents, dermatologists, and the in=
ternet, with many calling it out as unnecessary and potentially harmful to =
kids=E2=80=99 developing skin as well as their mental health.

- Rini faced serious backlash over its debut product, ~$7 animal-themed hyd=
rogel sheet masks for preschool-age kids, and its =E2=80=9Chealthy habits, =
spark confidence (https://heyrini.com/pages/about-us?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9eliz=
Ng9a0mxVXca4JaS5minyyZXB7Ye3FWFJM6vPSqB8sfx_m00OarhOzLHQ8RzgXdIV9QTLl5y4lT_=
ZKPBJx6Yx41Q&_hsmi=3D397065654 ) =E2=80=9D marketing language, which one cr=
itic who spoke to The New York Times called dystopian (https://www.nytimes.=
com/2025/11/15/style/skin-care-children-rini.html?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-9elizNg9=
a0mxVXca4JaS5minyyZXB7Ye3FWFJM6vPSqB8sfx_m00OarhOzLHQ8RzgXdIV9QTLl5y4lT_ZKP=
BJx6Yx41Q&_hsmi=3D397065654 ) .

But with adult skincare brands already making bank selling kids products me=
ant for more mature skin, these new companies argue they=E2=80=99re simply =
offering safer alternatives to products kids are already curious about.

Let=E2=80=99s just hope that, with the way things are going, =E2=80=9Cbaby =
botox=E2=80=9D doesn=E2=80=99t eventually take on a more literal meaning.

